Keeps the Home networks list of Intrusion Detection (Suricata) current
with the IPv6 prefix that your provider delegates to this firewall
(DHCPv6 prefix delegation).

When the delegated prefix changes and the Home networks list does not
follow, the IPv6 side of your network is no longer recognised as "home"
and rules that depend on HOME_NET silently stop matching. This plugin
adds the current prefix of the selected interface to the list and
replaces it when the prefix changes.

Optionally it also keeps the current IPv4 address of that interface in
the list, for providers that give the WAN a private address that is not
covered by your Home networks and changes from time to time.

The plugin is opt-in and only acts on a real change. It never restarts
Suricata (the rules are reloaded) and never touches the entries you
added yourself.

WWW: https://github.com/TBK27/os-dynamic-homenet

